# The scenes of the junit-temporary-folders deck, in order. Each "## Scene N: title" is one slide, spoken with item N of
# junit-temporary-folders.narration.md. Each line under a heading puts one thing on the slide:
#   note "<text>"         a line of text
#   show <file> ...       a code panel: <from> <to> or /pattern/, then a label; --mark and --zoom mark lines
#   run_live "<command>"  a live run, played from its cast in junit-temporary-folders.outputs/
#   callout "<text>"      a boxed sentence saying what a result means

## Scene 1: the export
note "The end-of-day *export*: the day's orders into orders.csv, in the folder it is given."
show OrdersExport 7 15 "the export" --zoom 13-14

## Scene 2: the code under test
note "The code under test: today's export. It meant to skip a cancelled order, but it returns."
show TodaysOrdersExport 11 25 "today's export" --zoom 18-20

## Scene 3: tests with a fixed folder
note "Tests with a *fixed folder*: both write to the same place, and nothing cleans it up."
show FixedFolderTest 14 36 "tests with a fixed folder" --zoom 18

## Scene 4: tests with a temporary folder
note "The same tests with *@TempDir*: each test gets its own empty folder, removed afterwards."
show TempDirTest 14 32 "tests with a temporary folder" --zoom 27

## Scene 5: the leftover file hides the bug
note "Run both sets of tests against today's export:"
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:junit-temporary-folders:test -Pcode=today"
callout "The fixed folder's leftover file hid the bug. The temporary folder was empty, so the test failed."

## Scene 6: the fixed export
note "The export that leaves cancelled orders out, and always writes the file:"
show FixedOrdersExport 11 19 "the fixed export" --zoom 16-17
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:junit-temporary-folders:test"
callout "Every test passes. Each one wrote, and read, only its own folder."
